  "notes": "Switchboard 1.24.0 — Background Items, missing-service detection, and verified updates.",
  "highlights": [
    "See what macOS runs in the background — Services adds a Background view of third-party LaunchAgents, LaunchDaemons, and login items, showing each one's permission, startup setting, and running state. It is part of the free Observer tool: turn Observer on in Tools to see it.",
    "Missing services are called out — a service whose Docker container, Homebrew formula, or launchd job no longer exists now reads Missing instead of Stopped, with a Missing filter and a Remove service action. Quitting Docker Desktop never marks a service Missing.",
    "Background items you can act on — an item that reliably matches one of your services shows that service's controls in the list; others offer Review & add or Manage in macOS. Items group by developer, and AI agents can read the same inventory."
  ],
